<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Combined and Joint Variation 4 - Name the variation (dropdown)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Decide which type of variation describes each situation. Choose the correct type from the drop-down menu below each one.</p>
<ol>
<li>{@st1@}<br>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</li>
<li>{@st2@}<br>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</li>
<li>{@st3@}<br>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</li>
<li>{@st4@}<br>[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</li>
<li>{@st5@}<br>[[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]] [[feedback:prt5]]</li>
<li>{@st6@}<br>[[input:ans6]] [[validation:ans6]] [[feedback:prt6]]</li>
<li>{@st7@}<br>[[input:ans7]] [[validation:ans7]] [[feedback:prt7]]</li>
<li>{@st8@}<br>[[input:ans8]] [[validation:ans8]] [[feedback:prt8]]</li>
</ol>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>To name a variation, ask two questions: <em>how many quantities</em> does the variable depend on, and does it change <em>in the same direction</em> as each of them or in the opposite direction?</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Direct variation:</strong> one quantity, same direction. Doubling one doubles the other: \(y = kx\).</li>
<li><strong>Inverse variation:</strong> one quantity, opposite direction. Doubling one halves the other: \(y = \dfrac{k}{x}\).</li>
<li><strong>Joint variation:</strong> two or more quantities, same direction with all of them, multiplied together: \(y = kxz\).</li>
<li><strong>Combined variation:</strong> two or more quantities, same direction with some and opposite direction with others: \(y = \dfrac{kx}{z}\). Look for "rises with … but falls with …".</li>
</ul>
<h4>The eight situations</h4>
<ol>
<li>{@st1@}<br><strong>{@lab1@} variation.</strong> {@why1@}</li>
<li>{@st2@}<br><strong>{@lab2@} variation.</strong> {@why2@}</li>
<li>{@st3@}<br><strong>{@lab3@} variation.</strong> {@why3@}</li>
<li>{@st4@}<br><strong>{@lab4@} variation.</strong> {@why4@}</li>
<li>{@st5@}<br><strong>{@lab5@} variation.</strong> {@why5@}</li>
<li>{@st6@}<br><strong>{@lab6@} variation.</strong> {@why6@}</li>
<li>{@st7@}<br><strong>{@lab7@} variation.</strong> {@why7@}</li>
<li>{@st8@}<br><strong>{@lab8@} variation.</strong> {@why8@}</li>
</ol>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
